WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.864
Begin with the actual P E endpoint and a credential reference authorized for

00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:06.165
the necessary reads.

00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:08.552
Add P C context when needed.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:12.539
Establish persistent certificate trust in the appliance and preserve the

00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:14.779
trust mount across container replacement.

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:18.138
The certificate must match the endpoint name or address.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:23.662
Upgrade Advisor now offers separate Verify T L S certificate controls for P

00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:27.715
E and P C inventory collection, enabled by default.

00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:31.982
A temporary exception is administrator-only, applies to that inventory

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:34.038
collection and resets afterward.

00:00:34.302 --> 00:00:37.843
The exception is audited and remains visible in saved inventory and

00:00:37.886 --> 00:00:38.910
assessment reports.

00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:42.920
Keep verification enabled for normal operation and correct the trust

00:00:43.006 --> 00:00:43.550
problem.

00:00:43.923 --> 00:00:48.148
This scoped inventory exception does not change drift, recovery or other

00:00:48.276 --> 00:00:49.705
workflow trust policies.

00:00:50.068 --> 00:00:53.985
Workstation connectivity alone does not establish access from the appliance.

00:00:54.482 --> 00:00:57.725
Open Upgrade Advisor and collect fresh inventory from the reviewed

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.429
connections.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:02.162
Inspect discovered versions and fields that remain unknown.

00:01:02.418 --> 00:01:06.599
Enter the intended target versions and supporting evidence, then run the

00:01:06.642 --> 00:01:07.310
assessment.

00:01:07.595 --> 00:01:11.456
Review blockers, warnings, unknowns and readiness actions.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:14.891
Save an immutable assessment snapshot for the change record.

00:01:15.232 --> 00:01:19.029
This read-only advisor does not run an upgrade or replace vendor

00:01:19.072 --> 00:01:21.082
compatibility and lifecycle checks.

00:01:21.431 --> 00:01:27.532
Save a desired configuration for D N S, N T P and Pulse with the correct

00:01:27.703 --> 00:01:29.282
cluster and credential reference.

00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:33.805
In Drift Detection select that file and Live Prism Element as the source,

00:01:34.061 --> 00:01:35.286
then run a manual check.

00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:38.368
Every live scheduled run collects fresh settings.

00:01:38.688 --> 00:01:41.248
Stored-snapshot comparisons are a separate mode.

00:01:41.462 --> 00:01:45.226
An unknown collection result must not be counted as a healthy match.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:49.682
Add or edit the Automation entry, choose the correct file, source and

00:01:49.725 --> 00:01:53.543
baseline, and review the five-field U T C cron expression.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:56.522
Save it enabled only after the manual check works.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:02:00.311
Inspect the next actual scheduled result and its timestamp.

00:02:00.588 --> 00:02:02.231
Pause schedules for maintenance.

00:02:02.508 --> 00:02:06.007
Editing or enabling an entry is not proof that a scheduled read has

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.150
completed successfully.

00:02:07.474 --> 00:02:10.930
A certificate trust failure requires the approved issuing chain or

00:02:11.015 --> 00:02:12.572
appropriate trust configuration.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:18.055
An I P or subject-alternative-name mismatch requires a matching endpoint or

00:02:18.098 --> 00:02:18.899
certificate.

00:02:19.232 --> 00:02:23.456
A network failure requires routing, firewall, name-resolution or

00:02:23.499 --> 00:02:26.080
target-service investigation from the appliance.

00:02:26.485 --> 00:02:29.776
These failures remain unknown, not drifted or matched.

00:02:30.122 --> 00:02:34.474
Do not disable verification or change the desired baseline just to obtain a

00:02:34.516 --> 00:02:35.242
green result.

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:39.807
Monitor and Verify links to Drift Detection, inventory and upgrade

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:42.799
readiness, and Execution History and Logs.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:47.711
Overview and Clusters now add explicit managed records and P E observations.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.627
These are separate evidence sources with different scopes.

00:02:51.082 --> 00:02:54.184
A P E observation becomes stale after fifteen minutes.

00:02:54.556 --> 00:02:59.206
Overview Refresh reads saved records; Collect P E health, read-only,

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.361
explicitly contacts the target.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:06.289
Review identity, full expected membership and reported health, then use the

00:03:06.332 --> 00:03:08.613
appropriate independent acceptance checks.

00:03:08.911 --> 00:03:13.007
N K P Validation Evidence remains under Advanced Automation with a Preview

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.991
badge and its retained sources.

00:03:15.397 --> 00:03:20.090
A specialist evidence pack, successful job or fresh P E Good result cannot

00:03:20.389 --> 00:03:23.459
independently declare a cluster ready for workloads.
